'''3.''' Belonging to or predicated of all the members of a class considered without exception: as, a ''universal'' rule. {{smaller|This meaning arose in logic, where it is called the complex sense of ''universal'', and has been common in Latin since the second century.}}
{{smaller block|Hearing applause and ''universal'' shout.
{{right|''Shak.'', M. of V., iii. 2. 144.}}}}

