{{smaller block|Set before your faith the freeness and the ''universality'' of the promise. Consider of God’s offer, and urging it upon all; and that he hath excepted from the conditional covenant no man in the world. {{right|''Baxter'', Saints’ Rest, iv. 4.}}
Another objection to all this remedy is, its want of ''universality.'' {{right|''Sterne'', Tristram Shandy, ix. 14.}}}}
